@startuml supervision_failure

title Supervision Failure

box "Main loop thread" #F0F4FA
participant "ProcessGroupManager" as PGM
participant "Graph" as Graph
participant "Transition" as Transition
end box

queue "Component Event Queue" as EventQueue

box "Alive supervision thread" #FAF0F4
participant "Alive Supervision" as Supervision
participant "RecoveryClient" as Recovery
end box

participant "Supervised Process" as Process

note over Graph: graph is in state kSuccess:\nthe Run Target is active

' --- detection ---------------------------------------------------------------
Process -> Supervision: alive indications
note right of Supervision
  Supervision was started for this process when the component
  was activated - see Component Activation.
end note

Supervision -> Supervision ++: check the supervision cycle

alt #F2FAF2 the indications arrive as configured
    note right of Supervision: nothing is reported, the next cycle is checked

else #Pink the configured tolerance is exceeded
    Supervision -> Recovery ++: request recovery for the component
    Recovery -> EventQueue: supervision failure of the component
    deactivate Recovery
    note right of Supervision
      Only the process identifier is reported. The supervision
      thread never touches the graph and never stops the process
      itself.
    end note
end
deactivate Supervision

' --- reaction ----------------------------------------------------------------
EventQueue -> PGM ++: component event
note over PGM
  The reaction to a supervision failure is currently always
  to request the fallback Run Target.
end note

alt #White the graph is in state kInTransition and target is not the fallback Run Target
    PGM -> Graph ++: Set fallback Run Target as pending Run Taret
    PGM -> Graph: cancel the running transition
    PGM -> Graph: set graph state to kAborting
    note over Graph
      kInTransition becomes kAborting: the components still in
      flight finish their current step and report back,
      components that are already running stay running.
    end note
    deactivate Graph

else #White the graph is in state kInTransition and target is the fallback Run Target
    note over PGM: nothing to do, the recovery is already underway

else #White the graph is not in state kInTransition
    PGM -> Graph ++: Set fallback Run Target as pending Run Target
    deactivate Graph
end

' --- recovery ----------------------------------------------------------------
PGM -> PGM: handle the graph state

alt the graph reaches kUndefinedState

  note over PGM
    The requested Run Target is only picked up once the graph has
    entered kUndefinedState, so a cancelled transition is
    first allowed to settle.
  end note

  PGM -> Graph ++: start a transition to the fallback Run Target
  Graph -> Transition ++: set up the transition
  Transition --> Graph --: components ready to be stopped
  note over Graph
    The failing component and everything that depends on it are
    stopped, then the fallback Run Target is started - see
    Component Deactivation and Component Activation.
  end note

end alt

deactivate Graph
deactivate PGM

legend bottom
  Alive supervision does not act on the process. It only reports, and the
  resulting Run Target transition is what stops and restarts the component.

  Should the process die as a result of its failure, this is reported
  independently through the OsHandler thread - see Process Termination.
end legend

@enduml
